IEC60870.NETAsync — Changelog
=============================

Changes to version 4.0.9
------------------------
- Raw protocol frame events: unified `RawFrameReceived` / `RawFrameSent` on IEC 104 client/server and IEC 101 client/server. Complete single frame (APDU for 104 incl. 0x68 APCI header; FT1.2 frame for 101 incl. start/control/checksum), delivered as a freshly-copied byte[] that is safe to keep/queue/log. Fires only when a subscriber is attached (zero overhead otherwise). IEC 104 receive side upgraded from raw TCP chunks to reassembled complete APDUs (ApduReader.Frame + ApduFramer.FrameParsedHandler). IEC 101 LinkLayerEngine bridges its existing RawMessageHandler hooks into modern events.
- New example: examples/cs104-client-raw shows subscribing to raw frames on both IEC 104 (default) and IEC 101 (--101) clients.
- Aligned all three package versions to 4.0.9 (Core, CS101, CS104).

Changes to version 4.0.7
------------------------
- ASDU god class split: ASDU.cs is now a thin facade; encoding moved to AsduEncoder, decoding + TypeID registry to AsduDecoder (new AsduDecoding.cs)
- TypeID registry is now the single source of truth for payload sizes and decode dispatch; fixed 3 size/dedispatch drifts (M_BO_TB_1 10->12, C_CS_NA_1 5->7, M_PS_NA_1 wrong class)
- GetEncodedSize() is now derived from the TypeID registry (base class default) instead of ~60 per-class hardcoded overrides; only variable-size types (FileSegment) keep an override
- Encoding path 0GC: value objects (CP16/24/32/56Time2a, ScaledValue, BinaryCounterReading, StatusAndStatusChangeDetection) gained AsSpan(); all frame.AppendBytes(GetEncodedValue()) calls switched to span-based AppendBytes(AsSpan())
- LinkLayer class renamed to LinkLayerEngine (removes namespace/type name clash, drops the LinkLayerType alias hack)
- CS104/CS101 timer loops: silent exception swallowing replaced with diagnostic output
- Target net6.0; same public API surface as 4.0.6

